Deep Handler composition
effect E3 { Op3 : () => Int; } effect E2 { Op2 : () => Int; } effect E1 { Op1 : () => Int; } sig h1 : (<E1> (() -> Int)) -> () -> Int fun h1(m)() { handle(m()) { case <Op1 => k> -> k(1) } } sig h2 : (<E2> (() -> Int)) -> () -> Int fun h2(m)() { handle(m()) { case <Op2 => k> -> k(2) } } sig h3 : (<E3> (() -> Int)) -> () -> Int fun h3(m)() { handle(m()) { case <Op3 => k> -> k(3) } } h1(fun() { h2(fun() { h3(fun() { do Op1 + do Op2 + do Op3 })() })() })()
stdout : 6 : Int

Deep operation clause can forward its operation to the enclosing handler
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } handle(handle(do Ask + 1) { case <Ask => k> -> k(do Ask + 1) }) { case <Ask => k> -> k(40) }
stdout : 42 : Int

Deep return clause runs in the enclosing handler's context
effect Reader { Ask : () => Int; } handle(handle(do Ask) { case <Ask => k> -> k(2) case n -> n + do Ask }) { case <Ask => k> -> k(40) }
stdout : 42 : Int

Resuming a forwarded operation runs the inner return clause
effect First { First : () => Int; } effect Second { Second : () => Int; } handle(handle(do First + do Second) { case <First => k> -> k(20) case n -> n + 1 }) { case <Second => k> -> k(21) }
stdout : 42 : Int

